{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-fermion-boson-knot-link","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:fermion-boson-knot-link","kind":"proposition","title":"Fermions are knots, bosons are links","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-borromean-baryon"],"tags":["fermion","boson","knot","link","torus-knot","component","reeb-flow","vertical"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Braiding.fermion_boson_knot_link","text":"fermion-boson-knot-link.md","leanSource":"fermion-boson-knot-link.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:fermion-boson-knot-link\"></a><p>The fermion--boson decomposition coincides with the knot--link decomposition of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,n)</code> torus family on Bring's surface:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A <strong>fermion</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha_V \\neq 0</code>) is a <strong>knot</strong> (1 component).</li>\n<li>A <strong>boson</strong> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha_V = 0</code>) is a <strong>link</strong> (2 components).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Equivalently, fermions have odd <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,n)</code> and bosons have even <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code>.</p>\n<p>The proposition classifies the two-strand torus family <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,n)</code> only. In the primary model the electron is the three-strand braid <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0 \\in B_3</code>, whose closure is the two-component positive Hopf link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,2)</code>; its fermionic statistics are not decided by this <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,n)</code> component-parity rule and remain an open derivation (whereas the single-component trefoil alternative <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T(2,3) = 3_1</code> sits at odd <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n = 3</code>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/fermion-boson-knot-link.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"9.5.11","page":"b/prop-fermion-boson-knot-link","qa":{"counts":{"pass":98,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":19,"unknown":0,"stale":23},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:fermion_iff_odd","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/fermion-boson-knot-link.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
